      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=6,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[-3X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[-3X] & =(-3)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =9\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =54.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
